<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Air France plane in Ireland after bomb scare.</title>
<headline>Air France plane in Ireland after bomb scare.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Air France Airbus with 229 people on board was diverted to Ireland's Shannon airport on Thursday because of a bomb scare, police said.</p>
<p>They said passengers were taken off the plane and the aircraft was taken to a safe area for a search.</p>
<p>The aircraft was on a scheduled flight from Paris to Mexico city when it was diverted to Shannon, Ireland's transatlantic flights terminus on the West Coast.</p>
<p>The search was expected to take some time, police said.</p>
<p>No further details were available.</p>
</text>
